// =============================================================================
// Detection: Failed sign-in spike from a single IP (password spray / brute force)
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   10+ failed sign-ins from ONE source IP within one fixed 10-minute clock bin
//   (bin() floors TimeGenerated to :00, :10, :20, ...; the output TimeGenerated
//   is the bin start). Two shapes fall out of the same query:
//     - many distinct users, few attempts each  -> password spray
//     - one user, many attempts                 -> brute force / credential stuffing
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   SigninLogs  (Microsoft Entra ID -> Diagnostic settings -> Log Analytics).
//   Covers interactive user sign-ins. For the non-interactive flood (legacy /
//   token replay) union AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs — see legacy-auth.kql
//   and break-glass-signin.kql for the union pattern.
//
// LICENSE
//   - SigninLogs export to Log Analytics requires Microsoft Entra ID P1 (or P2).
//     The free tier does NOT stream sign-in logs to a workspace.
//   - Runs as a Log Analytics scheduled query or a Microsoft Sentinel rule.
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - Shared egress NAT / corporate VPN / CGNAT can concentrate many users
//     behind one IP; allow-list known corporate egress IPs (a watchlist).
//   - A looping misconfigured client (old password cached) hammers one account
//     — real, but operational not malicious; tune the single-user threshold.
//   - MFA-required codes (e.g. 50074 / 50076) are "failures" but often benign
//     interrupts; the credential-failure filter below narrows to real misses.
//
// TUNABLE THRESHOLDS
//   FailureThreshold = 10 failures / IP / 10-minute clock bin. Window = 10m
//   (per task spec).
//   Known gap: the bins are tumbling, not sliding. A burst that straddles a
//   bin boundary splits (9 at 12:09 + 9 at 12:10 = 18 in about a minute) and
//   fires in neither bin. Change it in both twins at once (this file and
//   lab/splunk/detections/failed-signin-spike.spl): hopping 10m windows on a
//   5m step always catch 10+ failures that land inside any 5 minutes.
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   As deployed by lab/terraform/modules/monitoring: Frequency 5m · Lookback
//   1h · Trigger > 0 rows · Entities: IP=IPAddress only (UserList is a
//   dynamic array and cannot map to an Account entity). Suggested tuning
//   (not deployed): surface ErrorCodes in the incident for triage.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE (Logic App - lab/monitoring/playbook-notify.json)
//   Shared by all five rules, Sentinel path only (the post-trial Log
//   Analytics alerts just email the ag-identity-secops action group).
//   Incident created -> automation rule (lab/terraform/modules/monitoring) ->
//   (1) Teams adaptive card: incident severity, title, number, created time,
//       status, description and an "Open in Sentinel" link;
//   (2) ServiceNow incident: urgency/impact from severity (Medium -> 2),
//       category "inquiry"; (3) the INC number is commented back on the
//       Sentinel incident for the audit trail.
//   NOT BUILT (production follow-up): approval-gated Graph call to add the IP
//   to a CA named location / block list.
// =============================================================================

let FailureThreshold = 10;   // failed sign-ins from one IP in one Window bin
let Window = 10m;            // tumbling clock bin (:00, :10, ...), not sliding
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
// ResultType is a STRING in SigninLogs; "0" == success, anything else is a
// failed/aborted sign-in.
| where ResultType != "0"
// Optional: focus on real credential failures and drop benign MFA interrupts.
// 50126 invalid username/password · 50053 account locked (smart lockout)
// 50055 expired password · 50056 no/invalid password on record
// (Comment this back in to cut MFA-prompt noise; verify codes for your tenant.)
// | where ResultType in ("50126","50053","50055","50056")
| summarize
      FailedCount   = count(),
      TargetedUsers = dcount(UserPrincipalName),
      UserList      = make_set(UserPrincipalName, 25),
      ErrorCodes    = make_set(ResultType, 10),
      Apps          = make_set(AppDisplayName, 10),
      Country       = any(tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion)),
      FirstSeen     = min(TimeGenerated),
      LastSeen      = max(TimeGenerated)
    by IPAddress, bin(TimeGenerated, Window)
| where FailedCount >= FailureThreshold
| extend Pattern = iff(TargetedUsers >= 5, "likely password spray", "likely brute force")
| project TimeGenerated, IPAddress, Country, FailedCount, TargetedUsers, Pattern,
          UserList, ErrorCodes, Apps, FirstSeen, LastSeen
| sort by FailedCount desc
